    """Yield parseable coordinator records participating in ``wanted``.

    Index-free fallback for old log sets without a participant index.
    A document that cannot be parsed is skipped rather than raised: its
    participating logs are unreadable, so it cannot be proved to touch
    any log in ``wanted`` and is unrelated to this operation -- an
    unrelated corrupt registry record must never disturb it.  Records
    reached through a per-log index or a direct identifier stay strict.
